Hi Barsha,

If you are trying to read again the tabix files of methylRawDB or methylRawListDB objects you should be able to achieve this with the 'methRead ()' function, just provide the file paths to the tabix files instead of the raw files.

However , if you are trying to read tabix files for methylBaseDB or methylDiffDB, then you have to use the 'readMethylDB()' function. This actually requires that files have been created with version >= 1.13  of methylKit, where we started to write metadata into the header of the tabix files.

If these options don't work for you, please let me know.

Best,
Alex

